    dist: ["Hears voices during the day that comment on her", "She studies zoology"],
    model: "Soumya, 20, presents with isolated sleep paralysis with frightening hallucinations on waking: brief inability to move with a vivid sense of a presence. Irregular sleep and cultural stories of a sitting ghost (predisposing) shape both the risk and how she reads the experience; all-night study (precipitating) triggered more episodes. Avoiding sleep and lying on her back after late nights (perpetuating) make episodes more likely. No daytime psychotic symptoms and a supportive roommate (protective) are reassuring. Explaining what sleep paralysis is, regular sleep and less sleep deprivation usually help. The card about daytime voices is left out because she has none; that would point to psychosis. Her subject is a distractor. Frequent episodes with daytime sleepiness would need checking for narcolepsy.",
